{"input_text": "Question: How do we find a co-ordinate vector in Algebra? 
 For example, given: 
 $$ 
\begin{align*}
\left(\begin{matrix}
2 & -3 \\ 
0  & -4
\end{matrix}\right) & \left(\begin{matrix}
v_1 \\
v_2
\end{matrix}\right) = 0
\end{align*}
$$ 
 How do we calculate $ v_1 $ and $ v_2 $? 

Answer: $$ 
\begin{align*}
\left(\begin{matrix}
2 & -3 \\ 
0  & -4
\end{matrix}\right) & \left(\begin{matrix}
v_1 \\
v_2
\end{matrix}\right) = 0
\end{align*}\Rightarrow 
$$
$$\begin{align*}
\left(
\begin{matrix}
2v_1-3v_2 \\0v_1-4v_2
\end{matrix}
\right)=\left(\begin{matrix}
0 \\
0
\end{matrix}\right)
\end{align*}\Rightarrow$$
$$\begin{cases}2v_1-3v_2=0\\-4v_2=0\end{cases}\Rightarrow$$
$$\begin{cases}v_1=0\\v_2=0\end{cases}$$ 
