{"input_text": "Question: Is it possible to calculate $\sqrt{28 \cdot 29 \cdot 30 \cdot 31 +1}$ without any kind of electronic aid? 
 I tried to factor it using equations like $(x+y)^2=x^2+2xy+y^2$ but it didn't work. 

Answer: \begin{align}
&\text{Let }x=30
\\ \\
\therefore&\ \ \ \ \ \sqrt{(x-2)(x-1)x(x+1)+1}
\\ \\
&=\sqrt{[(x-2)(x+1)[(x-1)x]+1}
\\ \\
&=\sqrt{(x^2-x-2)((x^2-x)+1}
\\ \\
&=\sqrt{(x^2-x)^2-2(x^2-x)+1}
\\ \\
&=\sqrt{(x^2-x-1)^2}
\\
&=x^2-x-1
\\
&=30^2-30-1
\\
&=\boxed{869}
\end{align} 
